// Which pictures each ready-made wizard uses, in the order of `wizards.ron` (a wizard's place is the
// slot the game saves as its portrait). Each number is an entry of the original's file named in the
// comment; the client picks the file by the role. Read by the client; the rules do not know it.
//   portrait  wizards (the new-game picker)      mirror  moodwiz (diplomacy room, spell animations)
//   talk      diplomac (the wizard talking)      lab     wizlab (the wizard in the lab)
//   gem       lilwiz (first of its five colours) hall    halofam (the hall of fame)
//   summon    spellscr (the summon scene)        music   the wizard's place in the original's music order
//   win       win (arms rising)  hands  win (the hands held up)   lose  lose (the fall into limbo)
//   sphere, sphere_figure  spellose (Spell of Mastery lost)
//   stand, pieces, seize   conquest (a wizard destroyed)
//   parade, parade_rival   splmastr (the Spell of Mastery parade: the wizard, and a rival passing by)
[
    (id: "merlin", pictures: (portrait: 0, mirror: 0, talk: 24, lab: 0, gem: 0, hall: 1, summon: 46, music: 0, win: 3, hands: 17, lose: 1, sphere: 0, sphere_figure: 14, stand: 0, pieces: 18, seize: 33, parade: 14, parade_rival: 0)),
